# What the image does not need, and what it costs to send anyway.
#
# Without this the build context was 279 MB. Every `make` target builds the
# image, so every one of them tarred that up, copied it in, and then ran
# `chmod -R a+rwX /app` across it — a layer that took the best part of a
# minute and was invalidated by any edit, because `COPY . .` sits in front of
# it. Nothing here is used by the image, and most of it cannot be: the
# dependencies are installed inside it and the compose file masks them again
# with a volume.

# Installed in the image by `npm ci`, and masked by a volume at runtime. This
# alone is 223 of the 279 MB.
node_modules/

# History. The container reads the working tree, never the repository.
.git/

# Machine state: screenshots, baselines and diffs, rewritten by `make shots`.
.design-sync/.cache/

# Build output, written by the container and read back on the host.
storybook-static/
test-results/
playwright-report/
ds-bundle/
.ds-sync/
